7. How Do We Send Requests for Data Processing?

Using:

spark-submit

This command submits Spark applications to a cluster.

Basic Syntax
spark-submit app.py
Common Configuration Parameters
Application Name
--name EmployeeETL
Driver Memory
--driver-memory 4G
Executor Memory
--executor-memory 8G
Number of Executors
--num-executors 5
Executor Cores
--executor-cores 2
Deploy Mode
--deploy-mode cluster
Example
spark-submit \
--master yarn \
--deploy-mode cluster \
--num-executors 5 \
--executor-memory 8G \
--executor-cores 2 \
employee_etl.py
8. Spark Deployment Modes and Usage
1. Local Mode

Runs Spark on a single machine.

--master local[*]

Use for:

Learning
Development
Testing
2. Standalone Mode

Spark's own cluster manager.

--master spark://master:7077

Use for:

Small to medium clusters
3. YARN Mode

Runs Spark on Hadoop YARN.

--master yarn

Use for:

Hadoop environments
Enterprise systems
4. Kubernetes Mode

Runs Spark inside Kubernetes.

--master k8s://...

Use for:

Cloud-native deployments
Containerized environments
Deploy Modes
Client Mode
Driver → Local Machine
Executors → Cluster

Use when:

Debugging
Development
--deploy-mode client
Cluster Mode
Driver → Cluster
Executors → Cluster

Use when:

Production workloads
Long-running jobs
--deploy-mode cluster
